{"4587010": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Beggar's Road", "steam_appid": 4587010, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Survive the roads of 1407 Liège in a darkly comedic medieval roguelike of hard decisions and poor judgment.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're a beggar. A drifter. A nobody, with nothing. You wander the roads from town to town, forest to forest, and forgotten place to forgotten place in a world that is hard, petty, and sometimes silly. Gather poor companions, ration your meager supplies of food and gold, and make tough decisions as you attempt to survive each run.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Medieval engagements inspired by real medieval history: Pigs go to trial, relics are probably false, and a man might try to attack you with a knife over a turnip and think it's totally justified.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Travel a Living Medieval World</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Travel from handcrafted locations such as towns, market towns, forests, and ruins within the Prince-Bishopric of Liège. Each journey is an opportunity for new perils, new chances, and new people who you absolutely shouldn't trust.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/f80c717b11161004acb8211e7181d7c5.poster.avif?t=1782233200\" width=1010 height=222 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/f80c717b11161004acb8211e7181d7c5.webm?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/f80c717b11161004acb8211e7181d7c5.mp4?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Make Difficult (and Often Bad) Choices</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With every interaction, you'll make decisions. Some will be sensible, some will be moral, and some will be downright stupid. The decisions you make will affect your run, your party, and the mess that will inevitably ensue.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/9498c8c91b9cb20403e96f3da4bdeac9.poster.avif?t=1782233200\" width=1050 height=276 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/9498c8c91b9cb20403e96f3da4bdeac9.webm?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/9498c8c91b9cb20403e96f3da4bdeac9.mp4?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Recruit and Manage Your Party</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Assemble a party of beggars, vagrants, and scoundrels. Each will have their own strengths, as well as their own debts, troubles, and shady pasts.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/358bb47cd494e33e803cff4d2c1ecd05.poster.avif?t=1782233200\" width=1170 height=254 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/358bb47cd494e33e803cff4d2c1ecd05.webm?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/358bb47cd494e33e803cff4d2c1ecd05.mp4?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Balance Power Between Factions</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Manage the complex relationships between the Bishopric, the Merchant Guilds, and the Bandits:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Bishopric: power, order, and moral flexibility</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Merchant Guilds: wealth, power, and backroom deals</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bandits: freedom, violence, and strong opinions</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Support one, anger the others, or try to juggle all three. Carefully.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/760474bb1e343774bf2abe3684b6f79d.poster.avif?t=1782233200\" width=1124 height=502 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/760474bb1e343774bf2abe3684b6f79d.webm?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/760474bb1e343774bf2abe3684b6f79d.mp4?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Survive Each Run</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Manage your food, gold, and risks as you travel. Take risks for greater rewards, or play it safe and starve a little slower. Permadeath is a thing, but every run is a new story.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Survive the roads of 1407 Liège in a darkly comedic medieval roguelike of hard decisions and poor judgment.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're a beggar. A drifter. A nobody, with nothing. You wander the roads from town to town, forest to forest, and forgotten place to forgotten place in a world that is hard, petty, and sometimes silly. Gather poor companions, ration your meager supplies of food and gold, and make tough decisions as you attempt to survive each run.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Medieval engagements inspired by real medieval history: Pigs go to trial, relics are probably false, and a man might try to attack you with a knife over a turnip and think it's totally justified.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Travel a Living Medieval World</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Travel from handcrafted locations such as towns, market towns, forests, and ruins within the Prince-Bishopric of Liège. Each journey is an opportunity for new perils, new chances, and new people who you absolutely shouldn't trust.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/f80c717b11161004acb8211e7181d7c5.poster.avif?t=1782233200\" width=1010 height=222 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/f80c717b11161004acb8211e7181d7c5.webm?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/f80c717b11161004acb8211e7181d7c5.mp4?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Make Difficult (and Often Bad) Choices</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With every interaction, you'll make decisions. Some will be sensible, some will be moral, and some will be downright stupid. The decisions you make will affect your run, your party, and the mess that will inevitably ensue.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/9498c8c91b9cb20403e96f3da4bdeac9.poster.avif?t=1782233200\" width=1050 height=276 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/9498c8c91b9cb20403e96f3da4bdeac9.webm?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/9498c8c91b9cb20403e96f3da4bdeac9.mp4?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Recruit and Manage Your Party</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Assemble a party of beggars, vagrants, and scoundrels. Each will have their own strengths, as well as their own debts, troubles, and shady pasts.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/358bb47cd494e33e803cff4d2c1ecd05.poster.avif?t=1782233200\" width=1170 height=254 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/358bb47cd494e33e803cff4d2c1ecd05.webm?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/358bb47cd494e33e803cff4d2c1ecd05.mp4?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Balance Power Between Factions</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Manage the complex relationships between the Bishopric, the Merchant Guilds, and the Bandits:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Bishopric: power, order, and moral flexibility</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Merchant Guilds: wealth, power, and backroom deals</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bandits: freedom, violence, and strong opinions</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Support one, anger the others, or try to juggle all three. Carefully.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/760474bb1e343774bf2abe3684b6f79d.poster.avif?t=1782233200\" width=1124 height=502 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/760474bb1e343774bf2abe3684b6f79d.webm?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/extras/760474bb1e343774bf2abe3684b6f79d.mp4?t=1782233200\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Survive Each Run</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Manage your food, gold, and risks as you travel. Take risks for greater rewards, or play it safe and starve a little slower. Permadeath is a thing, but every run is a new story.</p>", "short_description": "A darkly comic medieval roguelike where you travel between towns, recruit desperate companions, and survive strange encounters through difficult choices, scarce resources, and shifting alliances with bishops, merchants, and bandits.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/d0e37da6f4febb5bb3755bd791afe481b0d516fc/header.jpg?t=1782233200", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/f9951771ce5a3ed7a76f806d1c515da1d56e4433/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1782233200", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4587010/f9951771ce5a3ed7a76f806d1c515da1d56e4433/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1782233200", "website": "https://beggarsroad.com/", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 (64-bit)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i3 or equivalent<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Integrated graphics (Intel HD 4000 or equivalent)<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 3 GB available space</li></ul>"}, "mac_requirements": [], "linux_requirements": [], "developers": ["Coldframe Studios"], "publishers": ["Coldframe Studio